in_vs_hist":0.10116766374493923,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.25935786896528135,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.10583655987993312,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":77.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05134370103405955,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":68.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03490111596131085,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":6.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.06507346589175499,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.037809998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":25.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Piper Sandler Companies operates as an investment bank and institutional securities firm that serves corporations, private equity groups, public entities, non-profit entities, and institutional investors in the United States and internationally. It offers investment banking services, institutional sales, and trading services for various equity and fixed income products; research services; advisory services, such as mergers and acquisitions, equity and debt financings, equity and debt private placements, debt capital markets advisory, restructuring and private capital advisory; municipal financial advisory and loan placement services; and various over-the-counter derivative products, as well as underwrites municipal issuances. The company also provides public finance investment banking services that focus on state and local governments, special districts and development infrastructure, project finance, and cultural and social service non-profit entities, as well as the education, healthcare, hospitality, senior living, housing, and transportation sectors. In addition, it offers equity and fixed income advisory and trade execution services for institutional investors, corporations, and government and non-profit entities. Further, the company has alternative asset management funds in merchant banking and healthcare to invest firm capital and to manage capital from outside investors; equity and debt capital markets products; public finance services; institutional brokerage services; fundamental equity and macro research services; alternative asset management strategies; and fixed income sales and trading solutions to banks, registered investment advisors, public entities, credit unions, asset managers, and insurance companies. The company was formerly known as Piper Jaffray Companies and changed its name to Piper Sandler Companies in January 2020. Piper Sandler Companies was founded in 1895 and is headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chad R. Abraham | Chairman & CEO | Age 56 | Compensation: $7.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $291K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $65K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Piper Sandler Companies is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.7B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 11% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $552M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.09\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -11.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 77\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2675525.04},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 17% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Piper Sandler Companies (NYSE:PIPR) President Debbra Schoneman Sells 39,708 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/piper-sandler-companies-nysepipr-president-debbra-schoneman-sells-39708-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793743964.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How (PIPR) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/39/How_PIPR_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_110326015802_1793689082.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793689082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Piper Sandler (PIPR) Stock May Be Overvalued Following New $200 Million Buyback","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-pipr/piper-sandler-companies/news/piper-sandler-pipr-stock-may-be-overvalued-following-new-200","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793686912.361,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.44,"tier":